cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AcousticScattering.jl in your work, please cite this software."
type: software
title: AcousticScattering.jl
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Lucca
    given-names: Brandyn
abstract: >-
  AcousticScattering.jl is a Julia package for modeling acoustic scattering
  and calculating scattering amplitudes and target strength. It provides
  modal-series, Kirchhoff, finite-element, boundary-element, and
  method-of-fundamental-solutions models for supported geometries and
  material configurations, including spheres, spheroids, and straight and
  bent cylinders. Optional Makie integration supports visualization of
  scattering responses, meshes, and acoustic fields.
repository-code: "https://github.com/brandynlucca/AcousticScattering.jl"
url: "https://brandynlucca.github.io/AcousticScattering.jl/"
# Software license. Logo artwork has separate terms in docs/src/assets/LICENSE.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - acoustic scattering
  - underwater acoustics
  - target strength
  - numerical modeling
  - Julia
